 "differences": [
  "Experiment 3 of the 20 deg study: the paper reports 10 of 10 participants with a significant aftereffect, these rows give 9: one participant has a wild last baseline trial (hand angle 2 deg for a 40 deg target) that inflates the baseline SD (11.8 deg) and brings z to 1.5; the authors presumably handled that trial differently. The other seven counts (10, 3, 9 in the 20 deg study; 6, 4, 7, 7 in the 90 deg study) reproduce exactly.",
